DP  - 2020 Mar
TI  - Comparison of the efficacy between NAC and metformin in treating PCOS patients: a 
      meta-analysis.
PG  - 204-210
LID - 10.1080/09513590.2019.1689553 [doi]
AB  - Our aim is to evaluate the clinical effectiveness and safety by comparing 
      N-acetyl-cysteine (NAC) with metformin administrated by polycystic ovary syndrome 
      (PCOS) patients. Systematic review and meta-analysis of randomized clinical 
      trials (RCTs). MEDLINE, EMBASE, Web of Science and China National Knowledge 
      Infrastructure were searched for studies. 10 studies were considered eligible for 
      inclusion. NAC significantly reduced BMI and total testosterone, there was no 
      significant difference in pregnancy rate, serum LH level, fasting insulin, and 
      LH/FSH ratio. In conclusions, NAC may be considered as an alternative supplement 
      to metformin, but large-scale randomized controlled trials are needed to assess 
      the efficacy and safety of NAC in PCOS patients.
