TI  - Comparison of body mass index and metabolic parameters with serum vaspin levels 
      in women with polycystic ovary syndrome.
PG  - 137-139
LID - S1871-4021(20)30009-6 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.dsx.2020.01.008 [doi]
AB  - This study showed that there is a positive correlation between serum Visceral 
      Adipose tissue derived Serine Protease Inhibitor (VASPIN) level and polycystic 
      ovary syndrome (PCOS). In previous studies, this relation was attributed to the 
      generalization of higher amount of adipose tissue in patients with PCOS. However, 
      we detected that VASPIN is significantly high in patients with PCOS regardless of 
      BMI. Besides, the metabolic parameters such as fasting insulin, HOMA-IR, 
      triglycerides and LDL-C levels were also increased in lean women with PCOS.
